11808	{"artifactId":"HLD-7e0ae92e8f3d3c3e","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-7e0ae92e8f3d3c3e-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-11T17:14:07.410Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every DEF acceptance criterion (S001–S005 ac1/ac2) is designed, and no DEF non-goal (DI2 project guideline activation, page/framework generation, copying UI UX Pro Max catalogs) is built.","evidence":"DEF.md:78-131 lists ten ACs. Each one appears in the HLD's verification matrix and has a contract behind it (sc1/sc2 publication gate, sc3 eligibility, sc4 coverage, sc5 gap/degraded, sc6/sc7 pinning and withdrawal). The DEF non-goals at DEF.md:52-54 are respected: the HLD hands guideline persistence to DI2 and authoring to DI3, and it builds no page generation or catalog copy.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"S003/ac1 coverage across ten named PRD domains × three UI types is designed as a publication gate.","evidence":"DEF.md:104 names the ten domains. The HLD's sc4 CoverageCell{domain,uiType,status:'pass'|'gap'}, the s3 boundary ('ten domains and three UI types') and the matrix line 'publication rejects any missing domain/platform cell, gap cell' cover it.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"src/analyze/docs-retrieval.ts Args require DbClient/closureRepos (repo-scoped), so it is a precedent, not a drop-in.","evidence":"docs-retrieval.ts:103-113: `interface DocsRetrievalArgs { readonly db: DbClient; ... readonly closureRepos: readonly string[]; ...}`. The cited line 115 is `maxResults`, which is inside the same interface.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"server.ts dispatches through the handlers map and serializes thrown errors as strings, so domain failures must travel as CorpusFailure values inside the result envelope.","evidence":"server.ts:187 `const handler = this.handlers[request.method]`; server.ts:196-197 `catch (err) { this.send(socket, { id: request.id, error: failureMessage(err, request.method) }) }`; failureMessage (server.ts:71-77) returns `err.message` / `String(err)`. Typed error codes would be lost, so the in-result union is needed.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"copy-assets.mjs copies src/assets recursively to out/assets, so src/assets/design-corpus/ would ship.","evidence":"copy-assets.mjs:28 `const DIRS = ['prompts', 'assets'];` and :39 `cpSync(src, dst, { recursive: true })`.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"PATHS in src/shared/paths.ts is the existing owner of ~/.insrc paths; PATHS.designCorpus is new.","evidence":"paths.ts:7 `export const PATHS = {` with insrc/config/lmdb/lance/... entries. There is no designCorpus key.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"JetBrains SettingsView needs no edit: settings-catalog derives groups from first-seen CONFIG_CATALOG order, and groupsOf consumes catalog.groups with a fallback for unlisted groups.","evidence":"settings-catalog.ts:76-80 builds `groups` from first-seen `opt.group`. SettingsView.kt:73-86 `fun groupsOf(catalog)` iterates `catalog.groups`, and its doc (lines 69-70) says unlisted groups fall into a trailing bucket so no option is dropped. A new 'Design intelligence' group renders without a Kotlin change.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s1 contract/validation code is described as proposed under src/design/corpus/.","evidence":"src/design/corpus/{contracts,canonical,validate,index}.ts already exist from the s1 build (commits 2477a0c8..bdbb7267). This is consistent with s1 owning them; the HLD's 'proposed' wording is only stale for s1. src/assets/design-corpus/ does not exist yet (Glob returned no files).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Adding designCorpus.enabled requires updating CONFIG_CATALOG, the catalog row-count assertion in config-catalog-contract.test.ts, and the vscode-plugin package.json mirror checked by manifest-catalog.test.ts.","evidence":"config-catalog-contract.test.ts:88-89 hard-codes `assert.equal(FROM_CONFIG.length, 37)`. manifest-catalog.test.ts:39-53 requires the declared insrc.* keys to EXACTLY cover CONFIG_CATALOG (it excludes only insrc.models.tasks.* and insrc.chat.*), and :55-69 checks type, default and scope 'machine'. The HLD names all three sites.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"s4 'updates the relevant Config type' for the new flag.","evidence":"No typed main-config interface exists. A grep for `export (interface|type) (Insrc)?Config\\b` across src/ returns nothing, and shared/types.ts has only provider/agent config types. Existing boolean flags are read ad hoc from raw JSON, e.g. gate.ts:147-148 `JSON.parse(readFileSync(PATHS.config,'utf8')) as { codeReview?: { enforce?: unknown } }; return raw.codeReview?.enforce === true;`. The change site the HLD names does not exist. [files: src/config/config-catalog.ts, src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts, src/shared/types.ts]","action":"Replace 'updates the relevant Config type' with the real reading pattern: a typed reader for designCorpus.enabled modeled on gate.ts:147, which treats anything other than `true` as disabled. Or state explicitly that s4 introduces the typed accessor.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The candidateContentDigest correction changes no public shapes and needs no migration of published data.","evidence":"No published corpus exists: src/assets/design-corpus/ is absent and no PATHS.designCorpus exists yet. The amendment (plans/design-intelligence-di1-s1-digest-amendment.md:18) says 'There are no published corpus releases to migrate; existing development fixtures and golden vectors must be regenerated'. ReleaseManifest/CoverageReport shapes are unchanged.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The normative digest order (candidate digest over the whole manifest minus releaseId/reviewDigest/coverage-entry digest; unique coverage entry or not computable) is what s1 implements.","evidence":"canonical.ts:95-103 still hashes only `records.map(({recordId, recordVersion}))` and `files.filter(f => f.path !== copy.coveragePath).map(({path, digest}))`. It drops label/createdAt/maintainer/role paths/mediaType, removes every coverage match rather than requiring exactly one, and never returns an empty value for zero or duplicate matches. The amendment's status line says 'implementation and BUILD completion are withheld'. The HLD calls this the normative rule but does not state that s1 code, fixtures and golden vectors must be reworked before s3/s4 consume candidate identity. [files: src/design/corpus/canonical.ts, plans/design-intelligence-di1-s1-digest-amendment.md]","action":"Add an explicit rollout note: s1 must re-implement candidateContentDigest per the amendment, regenerate candidate/review/release golden vectors, and add the missing/duplicate coverage-entry and role-swap regressions. That work has to be done before S001 is completed and before s3 produces CoverageReports bound to candidateContentDigest.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Catalog persistence is single-owned by S004 via sc7; S005 consumes sc7 and never writes catalog files, and DI2/DI3 state is not redesigned.","evidence":"§6.4 makes S004 the 'Sole owner of catalog file layout, serialized atomic commit, receipts and recovery via sc7'. §6.5 has S005 'Uses sc7 for all catalog/default/availability changes... not a second writer'. sc7 lists Owner s4 and Consumed by s5. DI2/DI3 appear only as consumers, which matches the non-goal at DEF.md:52.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each failure (invalid input, unavailable release, disabled flag, cursor invalidation, unsupported schema, conflict, validation, embedding failure) is detectable through IPC with a stated handling.","evidence":"sc5 defines a CorpusErrorCode union and a CorpusFailure{ok:false,error{code,message,retryable}} returned inside the result envelope. That is necessary because server.ts:196-197 stringifies thrown errors. Embedding failure gives `mode:'lexical'`/`status:'degraded'`. Withdrawn records return a CorpusReadResult `status:'withdrawn'` tombstone. Install/publish conflicts use 'conflict'/'validation-failed'. Crash recovery is stated in §3 (orphan registration without default, staging discard).","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion maps to a named test in the verification matrix.","evidence":"The §3 'Verification matrix' names a test for each of S001/ac1, S001/ac2, S002/ac1, S002/ac2, S003/ac1, S003/ac2, S004/ac1 (including the IPC and MCP round-trip), S004/ac2, S005/ac1 and S005/ac2 (N+1 and rollback). It adds crash-injection and idempotency tests. This matches the ten ACs at DEF.md:78-131.","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":2,"low":13,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-11T17:14:07.410Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{"change-sites.2":{"findingId":"change-sites.2","status":"resolved","note":"Corrected architectureShape: S004 introduces a typed designCorpus.enabled accessor using strict true semantics; no nonexistent main Config type is claimed. Public shapes and ownership remain unchanged.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-11T17:17:10.806Z"},"data-compatibility.2":{"findingId":"data-compatibility.2","status":"resolved","note":"Added explicit Phase A completion gate: current projected-pairs code is incomplete; amended hashing, regenerated independent vectors, role-swap and missing/duplicate coverage-entry regressions, and independent code review are required before S001 completion or S003/S004 consumption.","resolvedAt":"2026-10-11T17:17:10.808Z"}}}}}}
